<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov private machinery orders down 9.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov private machinery orders down 9.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's private-sector machinery orders, excluding those for machinery at electric power firms and for ships, fell a seasonally adjusted 9.7 percent in November from the previous month to 1.23 trillion yen, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Month-on-month percentage changes, seasonally adjusted, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			NOV		  OCT</p>
<p> Overall	    -3.6		+21.0</p>
<p> Private	    -9.7		+44.2</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			 NOV		  OCT</p>
<p> Public	    -23.3		+38.4</p>
<p> External	  +35.6		-20.4</p>
<p>Year-on-year percentage changes, not adjusted for seasonal factors, in different categories of machinery orders were as follows:</p>
<p>			NOV		  OCT</p>
<p> Overall	   +18.6		+27.4</p>
<p> Private	   +20.2		+34.1</p>
<p>(excluding ships, electric utilities)</p>
<p>			 NOV		  OCT</p>
<p> Public	     -3.7		+44.6</p>
<p> External	  +37.5		 -6.7</p>
</text>
